- net

' The foot at /io/mesa: the one place where a world meets Mesa.
'
' The foot holds the world's engine and its socket. These are not records.
' It holds no key. Mesa holds the world's key and the key it accepted for
' each peer, signs every page the world publishes, and checks every page a
' peer publishes. So a page the foot gets from a peer is that peer's page,
' and no rule here checks a signature.
'
' The foot keeps nothing a restart cannot make again. The first time a
' reader asks for a page, the foot derives it from the world's history.
' What a world holds of another world is in the store it keeps for that
' world, and in its own records beside that world's card.
'
' These are the foot's rules: steps over the foot's state and the world's
' state. The actor that owns the socket runs them and asks the world to
' make each change they ask for.
'
' A page is the bytes Mesa binds to one name and sends as fragments. The
' foot binds one page for each epic, each pin, and each slice of a page
' that is too long (mesa_foot/bind).
'
' An audience is the reader a published root is for. A world publishes one
' root to each peer, /<self>/our/<peer>, and one to every peer it knows,
' /<self>/our/public. The audience of a page from a peer's root is that
' peer's number. The audience of a page from the public root is 0.
' mesa_foot/mine gives the root of an audience, and the key that seals a
' page comes from the audience (mesa_foot/lock_of).
'
' The name of a page is publ/<kind>|<audience>|<x>|<y>.
'   e|aud|base|head   an epic of that root from version base (0: from
'                     nothing) to version head, without its records
'   p|aud|head|hash   the pin with that hash, shown in the epic at head
'   s|aud|page|n      slice n of a page too long for Mesa to send as one
'   h|aud|0|head      not a page: the name in a hint. It gives the version
'                     of a root
' A version is a stamp (net/stamp). So a name always refers to the same
' content, and a page does not change once the foot has bound it.
'
' Everything a world publishes to one peer is sealed for that peer. The two
' worlds share a secret that Mesa makes, on each side, from its own key and
' the other's accepted key. The secret stays in Mesa. The world seals a
' page of a peer's root with it and binds the page to its name. A reader
' asks for a pin of that root by a keyed alias of the pin's hash. So
' someone watching the wire learns no record, and cannot tell whether a
' guess at a record was right.
'
' Public content is sent as it is. Mesa signs every page, sealed or not.
+ mesa_foot
  + limits
    ' The sizes of a packet, a name and a fragment: Mesa's defaults. The
    ' signed-public profile sets a fragment to 1 KiB and a page to 1024
    ' fragments, so a longer name needs a larger packet. A larger value
    ' therefore travels as pins, and each pin is at most one page.
    ^ row[nat]
    [1472 256 1024]
  + domain
    ' The domain every world's name is in. In Mesa the domain is part of a
    ' name's identity.
    ^ nat
    | mesa_foot/tag "shrine"
  + bounds
    ' The engine's bounds, by Mesa's names: max_bindings, max_binding_bytes,
    ' max_reassembly_bytes and max_reads. They are larger than the defaults,
    ' which suit only a few pages. Then Mesa's retry policy at its defaults:
    ' retry_after, read_timeout and max_attempts. retry_after and read_timeout
    ' are in milliseconds, the unit the foot moves the engine forward in. An
    ' engine holds 64 MiB of bound pages, the most the bridge allows. After
    ' that the foot asks for a new engine (mesa_foot/effect/renew).
    ^ row[nat]
    [65536 67108864 67108864 1024 100 2000 4]
  + every
    ' How often the foot tells its peers the versions it has (tick), in
    ' milliseconds.
    ^ nat
    15000
  + name
    ' The name of a page in Mesa's signed-public space:
    ' publ/<kind>|<a>|<b>|<c>. One letter and three numbers. What they mean
    ' depends on the kind, and is said where each kind is used.
    \ kind=nat a=nat b=nat c=nat
    ^ nat
    | mesa_foot/tag (str/to_atom (str/cat_all ["publ/" (str/from_atom kind) "|" (nat/show a) "|" (nat/show b) "|" (nat/show c)]))
  + parse
    ' [kind a b c] from the name of a page, or no parts when the input is not a
    ' page name.
    \ named=nat
    ^ row[nat]
    = none=row[nat] []
    ? (lt (wid named) 9) none
    = text (str/from_atom (mod named (bex (mul 8 (dec (wid named))))))
      parts (str/split_byte 124 text)
    ? !(eq parts.len 4) none
    = head parts.at(0)
    ? !(eq head.len 6) none
    ? !(eq (str/slice 0 5 head) "publ/") none
    ?> (./some a) (nat/parse parts.at(1)) none
    ?> (./some b) (nat/parse parts.at(2)) none
    ?> (./some c) (nat/parse parts.at(3)) none
    [head.at(5) a b c]
  + most
    ' The most streams one epic may make a reader fetch, and the most bytes.
    ^ nat
    65536
  + room
    ^ nat
    268435456
  + page
    ' The most bytes the foot sends as one page. It is below Mesa's 1 MiB
    ' limit, which leaves room for a seal.
    ^ nat
    1000000
  + most_bytes
    ' The most bytes one page may have, in slices.
    ^ nat
    67108864
  + peer
    ' A world this world corresponds with, and that Mesa accepted a key for:
    ' its name and the number Mesa knows it by. The key is in Mesa.
    : world=iota id=nat
  + ask
    ' A page the foot asked for and has no answer to yet: the peer it asked and
    ' the parts of the page's name. `want` is the content hash the bytes of a
    ' pin must have. The name carries only an alias of that hash.
    : request=nat from=nat kind=nat aud=nat a=nat b=nat want=nat
  + stream
    ' The bytes of a pin as they arrived. The foot checked them against the
    ' hash that named them.
    : hash=nat bytes=nat
  + load
    ' An epic of one publisher's root while the foot gathers it:
    ' - the streams that arrived for it
    ' - the hashes the foot asked for and has no answer to yet
    ' - the hashes the foot still has to ask for
    '
    ' The foot asks for only a window of these at a time.
    : from=nat aud=nat epic=net/epic streams=row[mesa_foot/stream] wanted=row[nat] queued=row[nat] size=nat
  + lock
    ' What this world shares with one peer: a secret to seal with, a secret to
    ' make nonces from, and a secret to make name aliases with. Each is a
    ' handle on a secret that stays in Mesa.
    : id=nat seal=nat nonce=nat name=nat
  + long
    ' A page that arrives in slices: the ask it answers, its length, and the
    ' slices that have arrived so far.
    : ask=mesa_foot/ask mark=nat total=nat count=nat asked=nat got=row[mesa_foot/stream]
  + window
    ' The most pages of one epic the foot asks for at a time.
    ^ nat
    16
  + shown
    ' A pin this world showed to an audience in an epic it served.
    : bytes=nat
  + landing
    ' A landing the foot asked the world to admit.
    : request=nat from=nat aud=nat head=nat
  + change
    ' One change the foot asks the world to make.
    & mesa_foot/change/land
      mesa_foot/change/write
    + land
      ' Land this epic of this root of a peer (net/land). The card is where
      ' this world keeps where the root stands.
      : root=path card=path epic=net/epic
    + write
      ' Make this one write to a record of this world.
      : target=path change=writ
  + effect
    ' What the foot asks the actor that runs it to do.
    & mesa_foot/effect/send
      mesa_foot/effect/admit
      mesa_foot/effect/renew
    + send
      ' Send this packet, which the foot itself made, to a peer. The engine
      ' sends its own packets through the socket.
      : to=nat packet=nat
    + admit
      ' Ask the world to make a change. `request` is the number the foot
      ' knows the answer by (0: the foot waits for no answer).
      : request=nat change=mesa_foot/change
    + renew
      ' Give the foot a new engine: this one has no room left for a page.
      ' `era` is the number of the full engine (mesa_foot/foot), so the wire
      ' makes one new engine per full engine, not one per refused page.
      : era=nat
  + foot
    : self=iota rift=nat engine=nat endpoint=nat peers=row[mesa_foot/peer] next=nat
      asks=row[mesa_foot/ask] loads=row[mesa_foot/load]
      lands=row[mesa_foot/landing]
      bound=mop[path nat lt_pith] shown=mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith]
      told=mop[path nat lt_pith]
      locks=row[mesa_foot/lock] kept=mop[path nat lt_pith] longs=row[mesa_foot/long]
      whence=mop[path nat lt_pith] era=nat
  + turn
    ' What a step gives: the foot, and what it asks the actor to do.
    : foot=mesa_foot/foot does=row[mesa_foot/effect]
  + id
    ' The number Mesa knows a world by.
    \ world=iota
    ^ nat
    | quip_val world
  + start
    ' Makes a foot for a world from the engine and socket the wire made. The
    ' foot knows no peer yet (mesa_foot/meet).
    \ self=iota rift=nat engine=nat endpoint=nat
    ^ mesa_foot/foot
    = peers=row[mesa_foot/peer] []
      asks=row[mesa_foot/ask] []
      loads=row[mesa_foot/load] []
      lands=row[mesa_foot/landing] []
      bound=mop[path nat lt_pith] (mop/empty)
      shown=mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith] (mop/empty)
      told=mop[path nat lt_pith] (mop/empty)
      kept=mop[path nat lt_pith] (mop/empty)
      longs=row[mesa_foot/long] []
      whence=mop[path nat lt_pith] (mop/empty)
      locks=row[mesa_foot/lock] []
    | mesa_foot/foot self rift engine endpoint peers 1 asks loads lands bound shown told locks kept longs whence 0
  + meet
    ' Gives the foot the peers Mesa accepted a key for, and what this world
    ' shares with each.
    \ peers=row[mesa_foot/peer] locks=row[mesa_foot/lock] foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/foot
    | foot.set_peers(peers).set_locks(locks)
  + tag
    ' A word as bytes.
    \ text=nat
    ^ nat
    | add text (bex (mul 8 (wid text)))
  + lock_of
    ' What this world shares with a peer, or none when it shares nothing.
    \ id=nat foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ maybe[mesa_foot/lock]
    = none=maybe[mesa_foot/lock] .none
      found foot.locks.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/lock (eq item.id id)))
    ? !(found.len) none
    | ./some found.at(0)
  + veil
    ' The number a reader uses to ask for a pin. For a public root it is the
    ' pin's hash. For a peer's root it is a keyed alias of that hash.
    \ with=maybe[mesa_foot/lock] hash=nat
    ^ nat
    ?> (./some held) with hash
    | MesaVeil held.name hash
  + hashlike
    ' True if a number has the form of a content hash: 32 bytes.
    \ h=nat
    ^ bool
    ? !(eq 33 (wid h)) .false
    | eq 1 (load8 32 h)
  + wrap
    ' A page sealed for a peer and bound to its name. The nonce is made from
    ' the page and its name, with a key used only for nonces. So the same page
    ' under the same name gives the same bytes, and one nonce is never used for
    ' two contents.
    \ with=mesa_foot/lock spelled=nat page=nat
    ^ nat
    = made (Blake3Keyed (MesaVeil with.nonce (Sha256 page)) spelled)
      raw (mod made (bex 192))
      sealed (MesaSeal with.seal (add raw (bex 192)) spelled page)
    | add raw (lsh sealed 192)
  + unwrap
    ' The page inside sealed bytes. 0 when this peer did not seal them, the
    ' seal is not for this name, or the bytes were changed.
    \ with=mesa_foot/lock spelled=nat bytes=nat
    ^ nat
    ? (lt (wid bytes) 42) 0
    | MesaOpen with.seal (add (mod bytes (bex 192)) (bex 192)) spelled (rsh bytes 192)
  + raised
    ' The same foot on a new engine. The wire makes a new engine when the old
    ' one has no room left for a page. The new foot derives a bound page again
    ' the next time a reader asks for it. Reads in progress are dropped, and a
    ' later hint starts them again.
    \ engine=nat foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/foot
    = fresh (mesa_foot/start foot.self foot.rift engine foot.endpoint)
    | fresh.set_next(foot.next).set_lands(foot.lands).set_shown(foot.shown).set_told(foot.told).set_kept(foot.kept).set_peers(foot.peers).set_locks(foot.locks).set_era(foot.era.inc)
  + quiet
    \ foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = none=row[mesa_foot/effect] []
    | mesa_foot/turn foot none
  + peer_of
    \ id=nat foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ maybe[mesa_foot/peer]
    = none=maybe[mesa_foot/peer] .none
      found foot.peers.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/peer (eq item.id id)))
    ? !(found.len) none
    | ./some found.at(0)
  + mine
    ' The root this world publishes to an audience.
    \ aud=nat foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ maybe[path]
    = none=maybe[path] .none
      public=path [foot.self 'our 'public]
    ? (eq aud 0) (./some public)
    ?> (./some item) (mesa_foot/peer_of aud foot) none
    = pairwise=path [foot.self 'our item.world]
    | ./some pairwise
  + theirs
    ' A publisher's root as the publisher spells it: its root for this world,
    ' or its public root.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer public=bool foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ path
    = open=path [from.world 'our 'public]
      pairwise=path [from.world 'our foot.self]
    ? public open
    pairwise
  + card
    ' The path where this world keeps where a publisher's root stands. It is
    ' below the publisher's card and is not the card. The card says who the
    ' publisher is and where to reach it, and whoever decides that writes it.
    ' The foot writes only where the roots stand.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer public=bool foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ path
    = pairwise=path [foot.self 'io 'mesa from.world 'stand]
      open=path [foot.self 'io 'mesa from.world 'public]
    ? public open
    pairwise
  + head
    ' The version a root this world publishes is at, or 0 while the root holds
    ' no record.
    \ root=path state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ nat
    = case state.case(.z root).fall(0)
    ? (eq 0 case) 0
    | net/stamp foot.rift case
  + after
    ' Does one turn and then the next, and gives the two as one turn.
    \ first=mesa_foot/turn next={\ mesa_foot/foot}mesa_foot/turn
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = second (next first.foot)
    | mesa_foot/turn second.foot first.does.weld(second.does)
  + epic
    ' The change of a root between two of its versions, when this world can
    ' give it exactly: both versions are of this continuity and in this world's
    ' history.
    \ root=path base=nat head=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ maybe[net/epic]
    = w32 4294967296
      none=maybe[net/epic] .none
    ? !(eq (div head w32) foot.rift) none
    ? !((eq base 0) || (eq (div base w32) foot.rift)) none
    | net/delta foot.rift root (mod base w32) (mod head w32) state
  + spot
    \ aud=nat hash=nat
    ^ path
    [($u aud) ($u hash)]
  + parts
    ' A pin and every pin below it, as this world shows them to an audience.
    ' Each is filed under the number a reader uses to ask for it.
    \ aud=nat with=maybe[mesa_foot/lock] top=pin[any] out=mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith]
    ^ mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith]
    = at (mesa_foot/spot aud (mesa_foot/veil with (PinHash top)))
    ? out.has(at) out
    = kept out.put(at (mesa_foot/shown (PinBytes top)))
      inner=row[pin[any]] (PinParts top)
    | inner.fold kept
      \ acc=mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith] part=pin[any]
      ^ mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith]
      | mesa_foot/parts aud with part acc
  + show
    ' Keeps what an epic shows its audience: every record the epic names, and
    ' the pins those records hold. This is a cache. Anything not in it the foot
    ' derives again from the head in the name.
    \ aud=nat with=maybe[mesa_foot/lock] epic=net/epic out=mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith]
    ^ mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith]
    = fresh=mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith] (mop/empty)
      room (? (gt out.size 16384) fresh out)
    | epic.entries.fold room
      \ acc=mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith] item=net/entry
      ^ mop[path mesa_foot/shown lt_pith]
      ?> (./some record) item.record acc
      = held=pin[any] (pin record)
      | mesa_foot/parts aud with held acc
  + served
    : foot=mesa_foot/foot acts=row[row[nat]]
  + keep
    ' Keeps a long page for its slices, and the name it was bound under. The
    ' foot keeps the bytes of at most four long pages. It keeps each name as
    ' long as the engine does, because a bound name stays bound. With the name
    ' the foot can remake a page whose bytes it no longer keeps.
    \ at=path spelled=nat page=nat foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/foot
    = fresh=mop[path nat lt_pith] (mop/empty)
      room (? (gt foot.kept.size 3) fresh foot.kept)
    | foot.set_kept(room.put(at page)).set_whence(foot.whence.put(at spelled))
  + whole
    ' A long page, by the number its slices name it with. When the foot no
    ' longer keeps its bytes, it remakes the page from the name it was bound
    ' under and keeps it. A remade page is the same bytes: a name's content
    ' does not change, and a seal is made from the name.
    \ aud=nat hash=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ [page=maybe[nat] foot=mesa_foot/foot]
    = none=maybe[nat] .none
      at (mesa_foot/spot aud hash)
      had foot.kept.get(at)
    ? (maybe/is_some had) [had foot]
    ?> (./some spelled) foot.whence.get(at) [none foot]
    = [found next] (mesa_foot/made (mesa_foot/parse spelled) spelled state foot)
    ?> (./some page) found [none next]
    [found (mesa_foot/keep at spelled page next)]
  + made
    ' The page a name asks for, as the foot sends it. None when this world
    ' cannot serve that page. A page of a peer's root is sealed for that peer.
    ' If this world shares no key with the peer, the foot serves no part of
    ' that root.
    \ name=row[nat] spelled=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ [page=maybe[nat] foot=mesa_foot/foot]
    = none=maybe[nat] .none
    ? !(eq name.len 4) [none foot]
    = kind name.at(0)
      aud name.at(1)
      with (mesa_foot/lock_of aud foot)
    ? (and !(eq 0 aud) (maybe/is_none with)) [none foot]
    ?> (./some root) (mesa_foot/mine aud foot) [none foot]
    ? (eq kind 101)
      ?> (./some change) (mesa_foot/epic root name.at(2) name.at(3) state foot) [none foot]
      = sent=[base=nat head=nat lines=row[[rel=path stamp=nat hash=nat]]] (net/wired change)
        page (PinBytes (pin sent))
        shown (mesa_foot/show aud with change foot.shown)
      [(./some (mesa_foot/dress with spelled page)) foot.set_shown(shown)]
    ? !(eq kind 112) [none foot]
    = at (mesa_foot/spot aud name.at(3))
      known
        ? foot.shown.has(at) foot.shown
        ?> (./some all) (mesa_foot/epic root 0 name.at(2) state foot) foot.shown
        | mesa_foot/show aud with all foot.shown
    ?> (./some item) known.get(at) [none foot.set_shown(known)]
    [(./some (mesa_foot/dress with spelled item.bytes)) foot.set_shown(known)]
  + serve
    ' Binds the page a name asks for, the first time a reader asks. A slice is
    ' part of a long page (mesa_foot/whole). Any other page is made from its
    ' name (mesa_foot/made).
    \ name=row[nat] spelled=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/served
    = none=row[row[nat]] []
      idle (mesa_foot/served foot none)
      key=path [($u spelled)]
    ? foot.bound.has(key) idle
    = kind name.at(0)
      aud name.at(1)
    ? (and !(eq 0 aud) (maybe/is_none (mesa_foot/lock_of aud foot))) idle
    ? (eq kind 115)
      = [found held] (mesa_foot/whole aud name.at(2) state foot)
      ?> (./some whole) found (mesa_foot/served held none)
      = at (mul name.at(3) mesa_foot/page)
        total (dec (wid whole))
      ? (ge at total) (mesa_foot/served held none)
      = len (? (lt (sub total at) mesa_foot/page) (sub total at) mesa_foot/page)
      | mesa_foot/bind aud key spelled (add (loadvar at len whole) (bex (mul 8 len))) held
    = [found next] (mesa_foot/made name spelled state foot)
    ?> (./some page) found (mesa_foot/served next none)
    | mesa_foot/bind aud key spelled page next
  + dress
    ' A page as the foot sends it: sealed when there is a peer to seal it for.
    \ with=maybe[mesa_foot/lock] spelled=nat page=nat
    ^ nat
    ?> (./some held) with page
    | mesa_foot/wrap held spelled page
  + refused_call
    ' True if the engine refused a call outright.
    \ acts=row[row[nat]]
    ^ bool
    | acts.any((\ act=row[nat] (eq 5 act.at(0))))
  + bind
    ' Binds a page under its name. A page is the bytes Mesa binds to one name:
    ' here, an epic without its records, or one pin. Mesa sends one page as at
    ' most 1024 fragments of 1 KiB, and the foot's own limit is mesa_foot/page
    ' (1,000,000 bytes).
    '
    ' A page too long for Mesa to send as one is kept (mesa_foot/keep). Under
    ' its name the foot binds only its length and the number of slices. Each
    ' slice is bound when a reader asks for it (mesa_foot/whole). If the engine
    ' has no room left, the foot binds nothing and asks for a new engine. The
    ' reader asks again and the new engine binds the page.
    \ aud=nat key=path spelled=nat page=nat foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/served
    = none=row[row[nat]] []
      total (dec (wid page))
    ? (gt total mesa_foot/most_bytes) (mesa_foot/served foot none)
    ? (gt total mesa_foot/page)
      = count (div (add total (dec mesa_foot/page)) mesa_foot/page)
        holding (mesa_foot/keep (mesa_foot/spot aud (Sha256 spelled)) spelled page foot)
      | mesa_foot/bind aud key spelled (mesa_foot/slip total count) holding
    = ;acts (MesaBind foot.engine foot.endpoint spelled page)
    ? !(mesa_foot/refused_call acts) (mesa_foot/served foot.set_bound(foot.bound.put(key 1)) acts)
    | mesa_foot/served foot acts
  + slip
    ' The slip that stands in for a long page: sixteen bytes holding the word
    ' LONG, the page's length in bytes, and the number of slices.
    \ total=nat count=nat
    ^ nat
    | add (add "LONG" (lsh total 32)) (add (lsh count 96) (bex 128))
  + slipped
    ' True if bytes are such a slip. No real page is one: a stream starts with
    ' SILO and a sealed page is longer.
    \ bytes=nat
    ^ bool
    ? !(eq 17 (wid bytes)) .false
    | eq "LONG" (mod bytes (bex 32))
  + read_page
    ' Asks a peer for a page. When the name carries only an alias of the
    ' content hash, `want` is the hash the page's bytes must have.
    \ from=nat kind=nat aud=nat a=nat b=nat want=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = request foot.next
      ;acts (MesaRead foot.engine foot.endpoint request from (mesa_foot/name kind aud a b))
      asked foot.set_next(request.inc).set_asks(foot.asks.snoc((mesa_foot/ask request from kind aud a b want)))
    ? (mesa_foot/refused_call acts) (mesa_foot/finished request 1 0 state asked)
    | mesa_foot/acted acts state asked
  + acted
    ' Handles what an engine reports. It runs the step for each read that
    ' stopped, and asks for a new engine when the engine had no room left for a
    ' page.
    \ acts=row[row[nat]] state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = none=row[mesa_foot/effect] []
      full (acts.any((\ act=row[nat] (and (eq 5 act.at(0)) (eq act.at(3) (mesa_foot/tag "ResourceLimit"))))))
      first (mesa_foot/turn foot (? full none.snoc((mesa_foot/effect/renew foot.era)) none))
    | acts.fold first
      \ acc=mesa_foot/turn act=row[nat]
      ^ mesa_foot/turn
      ? !(eq 2 act.at(0)) acc
      | mesa_foot/after acc
        \ now=mesa_foot/foot
        ^ mesa_foot/turn
        | mesa_foot/finished act.at(1) act.at(2) act.at(3) state now
  + hint
    ' Tells a peer the version of the root published to it, and what this world
    ' holds of that peer's same root. The receiver does not believe a hint: it
    ' compares, then reads.
    \ to=mesa_foot/peer public=bool state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/effect
    = me (mesa_foot/id foot.self)
      root=path (? public [foot.self 'our 'public] [foot.self 'our to.world])
      offered (mesa_foot/head root state foot)
      held (net/held ['head] (mesa_foot/card to public foot) state)
      holds (mesa_foot/name 104 (? public 0 me) 0 held)
      offers (mesa_foot/name 104 (? public 0 to.id) 0 offered)
    | mesa_foot/effect/send to.id (MesaHint mesa_foot/domain me to.id holds offers 1 mesa_foot/limits)
  + mark
    ' What a hint to a peer carries, as one number.
    \ to=mesa_foot/peer public=bool state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ nat
    = root=path (? public [foot.self 'our 'public] [foot.self 'our to.world])
      w64 18446744073709551616
      offered (mesa_foot/head root state foot)
      held (net/held ['head] (mesa_foot/card to public foot) state)
    | add (mul offered w64) held
  + turned
    ' Runs after the world commits. It sends a hint to each peer whose roots
    ' changed since the foot last told it, or when what this world holds of
    ' that peer's roots changed.
    \ state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = both=row[bool] [.false .true]
    | foot.peers.fold (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
      \ acc=mesa_foot/turn item=mesa_foot/peer
      ^ mesa_foot/turn
      | both.fold acc
        \ had=mesa_foot/turn public=bool
        ^ mesa_foot/turn
        = at=path [($u item.id) ($u (? public 1 0))]
          now (mesa_foot/mark item public state had.foot)
        ? (eq now had.foot.told.get(at).fall(0)) had
        | mesa_foot/turn had.foot.set_told(had.foot.told.put(at now)) had.does.snoc((mesa_foot/hint item public state had.foot))
  + clock
    ' Runs as time passes. It lets the engine retry or give up on whatever it
    ' has in progress.
    \ now=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = ;acts (MesaAdvance foot.engine foot.endpoint now)
    | mesa_foot/acted acts state foot
  + tick
    ' Runs when it is time to repeat the versions the foot has. It tells every
    ' peer, which repairs a lost hint.
    \ now=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = moved (mesa_foot/clock now state foot)
      hints
        | moved.foot.peers.fold moved.does
          \ out=row[mesa_foot/effect] item=mesa_foot/peer
          ^ row[mesa_foot/effect]
          | out.snoc((mesa_foot/hint item .false state moved.foot)).snoc((mesa_foot/hint item .true state moved.foot))
    | mesa_foot/turn moved.foot hints
  + busy
    ' True if the foot already has part of a publisher's root in progress.
    \ from=nat aud=nat foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ bool
    ? (foot.asks.any((\ item=mesa_foot/ask (and (eq item.from from) (eq item.aud aud))))) .true
    ? (foot.loads.any((\ item=mesa_foot/load (and (eq item.from from) (eq item.aud aud))))) .true
    | foot.lands.any((\ item=mesa_foot/landing (and (eq item.from from) (eq item.aud aud))))
  + hinted
    ' Runs when a peer says what version its root for this world is at, and
    ' what it holds of this world's root. It reads the peer's root when that
    ' version is later than the held one and was not refused. It answers with a
    ' hint when the peer is behind on this world's root.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer holds=nat offers=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = me (mesa_foot/id foot.self)
      offered (mesa_foot/parse offers)
      held (mesa_foot/parse holds)
      sought
        ? !(eq offered.len 4) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
        ? !(eq offered.at(0) 104) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
        = aud offered.at(1)
          public (eq aud 0)
        ? !((eq aud 0) || (eq aud me)) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
        = card (mesa_foot/card from public foot)
        ? !(net/wants card offered.at(3) state) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
        ? (mesa_foot/busy from.id aud foot) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
        | mesa_foot/read_page from.id 101 aud (net/held ['head] card state) offered.at(3) 0 state foot
    ? !(eq held.len 4) sought
    ? !(eq held.at(0) 104) sought
    = aud held.at(1)
      public (eq aud 0)
    ? !((eq aud 0) || (eq aud from.id)) sought
    ?> (./some root) (mesa_foot/mine aud sought.foot) sought
    ? !(gt (mesa_foot/head root state sought.foot) held.at(3)) sought
    | mesa_foot/turn sought.foot sought.does.snoc((mesa_foot/hint from public state sought.foot))
  + heard
    ' Runs when a packet arrives.
    ' - a hint from a peer is compared (mesa_foot/hinted)
    ' - an ask from a peer is let through only for a name this world serves to
    '   that peer: the public root or the root published to it
    ' - every other packet goes to the engine
    '
    ' A packet from a sender Mesa accepted no key for is ignored, and so is a
    ' hint about a name that is not its sender's. The socket gives the sender
    ' from the packet's source address, and the link the engine knows that
    ' address by.
    \ from=nat link=nat packet=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    ? (eq from (mesa_foot/id foot.self)) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    = seen (MesaLook packet mesa_foot/limits)
      kind seen.at(0)
    ? (eq kind 9) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    ?> (./some sender) (mesa_foot/peer_of from foot) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    ? (and (eq kind 2) !(eq seen.at(4) from)) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    ? (eq kind 2) (mesa_foot/hinted sender seen.at(1) seen.at(2) state foot)
    ? !(eq kind 0) (mesa_foot/receive from link packet mesa_foot/none state foot)
    = name (mesa_foot/parse seen.at(1))
    ? !(eq name.len 4) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    ? !((eq name.at(1) 0) || (eq name.at(1) from)) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    = ready (mesa_foot/serve name seen.at(1) state foot)
    | mesa_foot/receive from link packet ready.acts state ready.foot
  + none
    ^ row[row[nat]]
    []
  + receive
    \ from=nat link=nat packet=nat before=row[row[nat]] state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = ;acts (MesaReceive foot.engine foot.endpoint from link packet)
    | mesa_foot/acted before.weld(acts) state foot
  + finished
    ' Runs when a read stops, with its page or without. A slice goes to the
    ' page it belongs to. A slip in place of a page starts the read of that
    ' page's slices. Otherwise the bytes are the page.
    \ request=nat status=nat bytes=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = found foot.asks.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/ask (eq item.request request)))
    ? !(found.len) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    = asked found.at(0)
      cleared foot.set_asks(foot.asks.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/ask !(eq item.request request))))
    ? (eq asked.kind 115) (mesa_foot/got_slice asked status bytes state cleared)
    ? (and (eq status 0) (mesa_foot/slipped bytes)) (mesa_foot/begin asked bytes state cleared)
    | mesa_foot/arrived asked status bytes state cleared
  + arrived
    ' Runs when a whole page arrives, or fails to. A page of a peer's root is
    ' opened with the key this world shares with that peer. A page that does
    ' not open counts as a page that did not arrive.
    \ asked=mesa_foot/ask status=nat bytes=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    ?> (./some sender) (mesa_foot/peer_of asked.from foot) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    = plain
        ? !(eq status 0) 0
        ? (eq 0 asked.aud) bytes
        ?> (./some with) (mesa_foot/lock_of asked.from foot) 0
        | mesa_foot/unwrap with (mesa_foot/name asked.kind asked.aud asked.a asked.b) bytes
      state_of (? (eq 0 plain) 1 status)
    ? (eq asked.kind 101) (mesa_foot/got_epic sender asked state_of plain state foot)
    | mesa_foot/got_pin sender asked state_of plain state foot
  + begin
    ' Runs when a slip arrives in place of a page. It asks for the page's
    ' slices, one window at a time.
    \ asked=mesa_foot/ask slip=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = total (mod (rsh slip 32) (bex 64))
      count (mod (rsh slip 96) (bex 32))
      mark (Sha256 (mesa_foot/name asked.kind asked.aud asked.a asked.b))
      none=row[mesa_foot/stream] []
    ? (gt total mesa_foot/most_bytes) (mesa_foot/arrived asked 1 0 state foot)
    ? !(eq count (div (add total (dec mesa_foot/page)) mesa_foot/page)) (mesa_foot/arrived asked 1 0 state foot)
    | mesa_foot/more (mesa_foot/long asked mark total count 0 none) state foot
  + more
    ' Asks for more slices of a long page, up to the window. The foot passed in
    ' does not hold this page. The foot given back does.
    \ reading=mesa_foot/long state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = flying (sub reading.asked reading.got.len)
      room (? (lt flying mesa_foot/window) (sub mesa_foot/window flying) 0)
      left (sub reading.count reading.asked)
      take (? (lt left room) left room)
      next reading.set_asked((add reading.asked take))
      holding foot.set_longs(foot.longs.snoc(next))
    % i=nat 0
      acc=mesa_foot/turn (mesa_foot/quiet holding)
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    ? (ge i take) acc
    | _ i.inc
      | mesa_foot/after acc
        \ now=mesa_foot/foot
        ^ mesa_foot/turn
        | mesa_foot/read_page reading.ask.from 115 reading.ask.aud reading.mark (add reading.asked i) 0 state now
  + got_slice
    ' Runs when a slice arrives, or fails to. When the last slice is in, it
    ' puts the page together in order and handles it as the page the slices
    ' are parts of.
    \ asked=mesa_foot/ask status=nat bytes=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = mine foot.longs.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/long (and (and (eq item.ask.from asked.from) (eq item.ask.aud asked.aud)) (eq item.mark asked.a))))
    ? !(mine.len) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    = reading mine.at(0)
      rest foot.set_longs(foot.longs.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/long !(and (and (eq item.ask.from asked.from) (eq item.ask.aud asked.aud)) (eq item.mark asked.a)))))
    ? !(eq status 0) (mesa_foot/arrived reading.ask 1 0 state rest)
    = got reading.got.snoc((mesa_foot/stream asked.b bytes))
      next reading.set_got(got)
    ? (lt got.len reading.count) (mesa_foot/more next state rest)
    = whole (mesa_foot/joined got reading.count)
    ? !(eq (dec (wid whole)) reading.total) (mesa_foot/arrived reading.ask 1 0 state rest)
    | mesa_foot/arrived reading.ask 0 whole state rest
  + joined
    ' The slices joined in order, as one run of bytes. It builds a byte tree of
    ' the slices (bat_concat) and the runtime flattens it in one pass. So the
    ' work grows with the number of bytes, with no big-number arithmetic per
    ' slice.
    \ got=row[mesa_foot/stream] count=nat
    ^ nat
    % i=nat 0
      parts=row[any] []
    ^ nat
    ? (ge i count) (mesa_foot/flat parts)
    = found got.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/stream (eq item.hash i)))
    ? !(found.len) (mesa_foot/flat parts)
    | _ i.inc parts.snoc((bat_bar found.at(0).bytes))
  + flat
    ' The bytes of a row of byte trees as one bar: the bytes, then the byte 1
    ' that marks where they end.
    \ parts=row[any]
    ^ nat
    | bat_flatten (bat_concat parts.snoc((bat_bytes 1 1)))
  + refused
    ' Records that a head was refused, and why, beside where the root stands.
    ' The foot then does not ask for that head again.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer public=bool head=nat why=iota state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = [target change] (net/refuse (mesa_foot/card from public foot) head why state)
      does=row[mesa_foot/effect] [(mesa_foot/effect/admit 0 (mesa_foot/change/write target change))]
    | mesa_foot/turn foot does
  + got_epic
    ' Runs when an epic arrives, without its records. Mesa checked the page as
    ' its publisher's page under that name. The foot assumes nothing else about
    ' the bytes: they must be an epic, and the one it asked for. It then asks
    ' for each record this world lacks, by the record's hash. A publisher that
    ' cannot give the change from the version this world is at sends no page,
    ' and the foot then asks it for the whole root.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer asked=mesa_foot/ask status=nat bytes=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = public (eq asked.aud 0)
      idle (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    ? !(eq status 0)
      ? (eq asked.a 0) idle
      | mesa_foot/read_page from.id 101 asked.aud 0 asked.b 0 state foot
    = stored=maybe[pin[any]] (PinFrom bytes)
    ?> (./some held) stored idle
    ?> (./some change) (net/read (unpin held)) idle
    ? !(and (eq change.base asked.a) (eq change.head asked.b)) idle
    ? !(change.entries.all((\ item=net/entry ((eq 0 item.hash) || (mesa_foot/hashlike item.hash))))) idle
    = card (mesa_foot/card from public foot)
      root (mesa_foot/theirs from public foot)
    = lacking (net/lacks root change state)
      streams=row[mesa_foot/stream] []
      nothing=row[nat] []
      fresh (mesa_foot/load from.id asked.aud change streams nothing lacking 0)
    | mesa_foot/pump from fresh state foot
  + without
    ' Keeps only the loads that are not for one publisher's root.
    \ from=nat aud=nat foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/foot
    | foot.set_loads(foot.loads.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/load !(and (eq item.from from) (eq item.aud aud)))))
  + got_pin
    ' Runs when the bytes of a pin arrive. They must hash to the name the foot
    ' asked by. The foot then asks for each pin the bytes name. When none is
    ' left, the epic is complete. When a page does not arrive, the foot drops
    ' this epic and a later hint starts it again.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer asked=mesa_foot/ask status=nat bytes=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = public (eq asked.aud 0)
      held foot.loads.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/load (and (and (eq item.from asked.from) (eq item.aud asked.aud)) (eq item.epic.head asked.a))))
    ? !(held.len) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    = gathering held.at(0)
      rest (mesa_foot/without asked.from asked.aud foot)
    ? !(eq status 0) (mesa_foot/quiet rest)
    ? !(eq (Sha256 bytes) asked.want) (mesa_foot/refused from public asked.a 'net_unfit state rest)
    = streams=row[mesa_foot/stream] gathering.streams.snoc((mesa_foot/stream asked.want bytes))
      size (add gathering.size (wid bytes))
    ? (gt streams.len mesa_foot/most) (mesa_foot/refused from public asked.a 'net_unfit state rest)
    ? (gt size mesa_foot/room) (mesa_foot/refused from public asked.a 'net_unfit state rest)
    = still=row[nat] gathering.wanted.keep((\ hash=nat !(eq hash asked.want)))
      named=row[nat] (PinNames bytes)
      more=row[nat]
        | named.keep
          \ hash=nat
          ^ bool
          ? (streams.any((\ item=mesa_foot/stream (eq item.hash hash)))) .false
          ? (still.any((\ seen=nat (eq seen hash)))) .false
          ? (gathering.queued.any((\ seen=nat (eq seen hash)))) .false
          .true
      next gathering.set_streams(streams).set_wanted(still).set_queued(gathering.queued.weld(more)).set_size(size)
    | mesa_foot/pump from next state rest
  + pump
    ' Asks for more of an epic's pages, up to the window. When the foot waits
    ' for no page and has none left to ask for, the epic is complete. The foot
    ' passed in does not hold this load. The foot given back holds it as it is
    ' now.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer gathering=mesa_foot/load state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = room (? (lt gathering.wanted.len mesa_foot/window) (sub mesa_foot/window gathering.wanted.len) 0)
      count (? (lt gathering.queued.len room) gathering.queued.len room)
      asking=row[nat] gathering.queued.take(count)
      next gathering.set_wanted(gathering.wanted.weld(asking)).set_queued(gathering.queued.drop(count))
      loading foot.set_loads(foot.loads.snoc(next))
      open=maybe[mesa_foot/lock] .none
      with (? (eq 0 gathering.aud) open (mesa_foot/lock_of from.id foot))
    ? (and (eq 0 next.wanted.len) (eq 0 next.queued.len)) (mesa_foot/complete from next state loading)
    | asking.fold (mesa_foot/quiet loading)
      \ acc=mesa_foot/turn hash=nat
      ^ mesa_foot/turn
      | mesa_foot/after acc
        \ now=mesa_foot/foot
        ^ mesa_foot/turn
        | mesa_foot/read_page from.id 112 gathering.aud gathering.epic.head (mesa_foot/veil with hash) hash state now
  + staged
    ' True if a stream can load into the store now. A stream loads after every
    ' pin it names has loaded. A stream that holds code does not load.
    \ bytes=nat
    ^ bool
    = found=maybe[pin[any]] (PinFrom bytes)
    | maybe/is_some found
  + rebuild
    ' Loads every stream, a pin's parts before the pin. Parts arrive after the
    ' pin that names them, so the last streams to arrive go first. Whatever a
    ' pass does not load is tried again, for as long as a pass loads something.
    \ streams=row[mesa_foot/stream]
    ^ bool
    % left=row[mesa_foot/stream] streams.rev
    ^ bool
    ? !(left.len) .true
    = ;after (left.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/stream !(mesa_foot/staged item.bytes))))
    ? (eq after.len left.len) .false
    | _ after
  + record
    ' The record a stream holds, when it holds one.
    \ bytes=nat
    ^ maybe[myth]
    = none=maybe[myth] .none
      found=maybe[pin[any]] (PinFrom bytes)
    ?> (./some held) found none
    | net/sound (unpin held)
  + complete
    ' Runs once all the streams of an epic have arrived. It remakes the epic's
    ' pins, puts each record where the epic names its hash, and asks the world
    ' to land the epic as one event.
    \ from=mesa_foot/peer gathered=mesa_foot/load state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = public (eq gathered.aud 0)
      rest (mesa_foot/without gathered.from gathered.aud foot)
      head gathered.epic.head
      ;whole (mesa_foot/rebuild gathered.streams)
    ? !whole (mesa_foot/refused from public head 'net_unfit state rest)
    = start=maybe[net/epic] (./some gathered.epic)
      none=maybe[net/epic] .none
      filled
        | gathered.epic.entries.fold start
          \ acc=maybe[net/epic] item=net/entry
          ^ maybe[net/epic]
          ?> (./some change) acc none
          ? (eq 0 item.hash) acc
          = found gathered.streams.keep((\ got=mesa_foot/stream (eq got.hash item.hash)))
          ? !(found.len) acc
          ?> (./some record) (mesa_foot/record found.at(0).bytes) none
          | ./some (net/given item.hash record change)
    ?> (./some change) filled (mesa_foot/refused from public head 'net_unfit state rest)
    = root (mesa_foot/theirs from public foot)
      card (mesa_foot/card from public foot)
      request rest.next
      waiting rest.set_next(request.inc).set_lands(rest.lands.snoc((mesa_foot/landing request gathered.from gathered.aud head)))
      does=row[mesa_foot/effect] [(mesa_foot/effect/admit request (mesa_foot/change/land root card change))]
    | mesa_foot/turn waiting does
  + landed
    ' Runs when the world answers a landing. If the world refused it, the
    ' reason is recorded beside where the root stands. In three cases nothing
    ' is recorded and a later hint starts again: the epic was a repeat, the
    ' epic did not start where the root stands, or the publisher's store moved
    ' after the plan was made.
    \ request=nat why=maybe[iota] state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_foot/turn
    = found foot.lands.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/landing (eq item.request request)))
    ? !(found.len) (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
    = was found.at(0)
      cleared foot.set_lands(foot.lands.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/landing !(eq item.request request))))
    ?> (./some reason) why (mesa_foot/quiet cleared)
    ? (eq_iota reason 'net_stale) (mesa_foot/quiet cleared)
    ? (eq_iota reason 'net_gap) (mesa_foot/quiet cleared)
    ? (eq_iota reason 'peer_store_moved) (mesa_foot/quiet cleared)
    ?> (./some sender) (mesa_foot/peer_of was.from cleared) (mesa_foot/quiet cleared)
    | mesa_foot/refused sender (eq was.aud 0) was.head reason state cleared
